{"content_hash": "c944f97692891e07", "version_id": 662, "article_id": 67, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Bank of America pays $1.2bn fine over money-laundering", "title_zh": "美国银行因反洗钱不力被罚12亿美元", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "guardian_business", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/14/bank-of-america-fined-money-laundering", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1527874594978-ee4f8a05b4c1?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8YmFuayUyMGFtZXJpY2ElMjBmaW5lZHxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkyMDIyNTY4fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Melinda Gimpel on Unsplash", "author": "Melinda Gimpel", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@melindagimpel?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/petition-to-file-for-bankruptcy-9j8k3l9afkc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(122, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(160, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "04b2441ba82d"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-15", "word_count": 113, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "Bank of America must pay a big fine. US regulators say the bank failed to report suspicious money activity.", "lead_zh": "美国银行要交一大笔罚款。美国监管机构说，这家银行没有报告可疑的资金活动。", "preview": "Bank of America was fined $1.21bn by US regulators. The bank failed to report over $5bn in suspicious activity. This is the third-largest fi", "preview_zh": "美国银行被美国监管机构罚款12.1亿美元。这家银行没有报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动。这是美国财政部历史上第三大罚款。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 651, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 49.2, "size_bytes": 296208, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 138, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_a2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 50.225, "size_bytes": 302256, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 138, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_a2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_a2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 53.2, "size_bytes": 320112, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 138, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_a2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_a2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 46.2, "size_bytes": 278208, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 138, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_a2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/67/en_a2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 49.95, "size_bytes": 300672, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 138, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/67/en_a2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@2e11152/content/data/versions/662.json", "paragraphs": ["Bank of America was fined $1.21bn by US regulators. The bank failed to report over $5bn in suspicious activity. This is the third-largest fine in US treasury history.", "The treasury said the bank cared more about money than safety. Bank of America will hire a third party to check past transactions. The bank said the fine will cut its third-quarter earnings.", "The bank will take a $1.2bn charge. This will reduce net income by about 17 cents a share. Shares fell 2.7% in after-hours trading.", "The fine includes a $750m civil penalty from the OCC. The bank also paid $11.6m for sanctions violations. This happened days after American Express got a $350m fine."], "paragraphs_zh": ["美国银行被美国监管机构罚款12.1亿美元。这家银行没有报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动。这是美国财政部历史上第三大罚款。", "财政部说，这家银行更关心钱，而不是安全。美国银行将聘请第三方来检查过去的交易。银行说，这笔罚款会减少第三季度的收益。", "该银行将承担12亿美元的支出。这将使净利润每股减少约17美分。盘后交易中股价下跌了2.7%。", "这笔罚款包括来自OCC的7.5亿美元民事罚款。该银行还因违反制裁支付了1160万美元。此事发生在美国运通被罚3.5亿美元几天后。"], "body": "Bank of America was fined $1.21bn by US regulators. The bank failed to report over $5bn in suspicious activity. This is the third-largest fine in US treasury history.\n\nThe treasury said the bank cared more about money than safety. Bank of America will hire a third party to check past transactions. The bank said the fine will cut its third-quarter earnings.\n\nThe bank will take a $1.2bn charge. This will reduce net income by about 17 cents a share. Shares fell 2.7% in after-hours trading.\n\nThe fine includes a $750m civil penalty from the OCC. The bank also paid $11.6m for sanctions violations. This happened days after American Express got a $350m fine.", "body_zh": "美国银行被美国监管机构罚款12.1亿美元。这家银行没有报告超过50亿美元的可疑活动。这是美国财政部历史上第三大罚款。\n\n财政部说，这家银行更关心钱，而不是安全。美国银行将聘请第三方来检查过去的交易。银行说，这笔罚款会减少第三季度的收益。\n\n该银行将承担12亿美元的支出。这将使净利润每股减少约17美分。盘后交易中股价下跌了2.7%。\n\n这笔罚款包括来自OCC的7.5亿美元民事罚款。该银行还因违反制裁支付了1160万美元。此事发生在美国运通被罚3.5亿美元几天后。", "text": "Bank of America was fined $1.21bn by US regulators. The bank failed to report over $5bn in suspicious activity. This is the third-largest fine in US treasury history. The treasury said the bank cared more about money than safety. Bank of America will hire a third party to check past transactions. The bank said the fine will cut its third-quarter earnings. The bank will take a $1.2bn charge. This will reduce net income by about 17 cents a share. Shares fell 2.7% in after-hours trading. The fine includes a $750m civil penalty from the OCC. The bank also paid $11.6m for sanctions violations. This happened days after American Express got a $350m fine.", "vocab": [{"word": "fine", "pos": "noun", "zh": "罚款", "note": "动词也可表示“罚款”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "regulator", "pos": "noun", "zh": "监管机构", "note": "常指政府监管部门", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "report", "pos": "verb", "zh": "报告", "note": "向官方报告信息", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "suspicious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "可疑的", "note": "形容看起来不对劲的事物", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "treasury", "pos": "noun", "zh": "财政部", "note": "美国财政部", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "earnings", "pos": "noun", "zh": "收益", "note": "公司赚的钱", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "share", "pos": "noun", "zh": "股份", "note": "公司股票的一部分", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "penalty", "pos": "noun", "zh": "处罚", "note": "因违规而受到的惩罚", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn for money-laundering failures", "summary_original": "Third-largest fine in US treasury’s history, due to failure to report suspicious activity, may affect third-quarter earnings\nBank of America\n(BAC.N), has been fined $1.21bn by US regulators for widespread failures to detect ‌potential money laundering and other illicit activity, a penalty the bank said will hurt third-quarter earnings.\nThe US treasury department said the fine, the third-largest in department history, is due to the bank’s failure to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity to the government, including $1bn that posed national security-related and other priority illicit finance risks.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Bank of America fined $1.2bn for money-laundering failures\nThird-largest fine in US treasury’s history, due to failure to report suspicious activity, may affect third-quarter earnings\nBank of America\n(BAC.N), has been fined $1.21bn by US regulators for widespread failures to detect ‌potential money laundering and other illicit activity, a penalty the bank said will hurt third-quarter earnings.\nThe US treasury department said the fine, the third-largest in department history, is due to the bank’s failure to report more than $5bn in suspicious activity to the government, including $1bn that posed national security-related and other priority illicit finance risks.\n“Financial institutions are on the ​front lines of protecting our economic and national security,” the treasury secretary, Scott Bessent, said in a statement. “When a bank of this size ​fails to meet its anti-money laundering and sanctions obligations, the consequences extend far beyond its own walls, exposing the ⁠entire US financial system to significant illicit finance risks.”\nThe treasury said the bank “prioritized its revenues” in building compliance programs, and overly relied on inquiries ​from outside parties such as law enforcement and other financial institutions instead of its own internal controls.\nThe consent order requires\nBank of America\nto hire an ​independent third party to review past transactions, identify suspicious activity that the bank failed to detect at the time and report those transactions to the treasury department’s Financial Crimes Enforcement Network.\n“Financial crime compliance is serious, and we are responsible for getting it right,” said a Bank of America spokesperson in a statement. “We have invested billions of dollars in technology and dedicated thousands of ​employees to combat financial crime, and our team is far along with and committed to completing the work required to address the issues raised ​by our regulators.”\nThe spokesperson added that the bank’s third-quarter results due for release on Wednesday would include a non-tax-deductible charge of $1.2bn, which will reduce quarterly net income ‌by approximately ⁠17 cents a share.\nAnalysts have estimated adjusted earnings per share of $1.10, according to mean estimates compiled by LSEG, but that excludes one-offs like this fine.\nShares were down 2.7% in after-hours trading after closing the day down 1.1%.\nThe penalty is likely to add to negative investor sentiment and raise concerns about higher expenses and whether Bank of America can maintain its roughly $6bn quarterly share buyback pace, the UBS analyst Erika Najarian said in a note.\nWith earnings due ​on Wednesday, “we think shares likely underperforming at ​open”, she said.\nShe noted there ⁠was no asset cap, a regulatory penalty that would limit how large the bank could grow.\nAs part of the fine, the treasury department’s office of the comptroller of the currency levied a $750m civil ​penalty against the lender, the largest ever for the regulator, citing failures to address shortcomings in its anti-money ​laundering programs that were ⁠identified as part of a 2024 cease-and-desist order from the watchdog.\nThe regulator said the bank’s compliance program was “deficient and ineffective”, and its transaction monitoring system caused the bank to delay filing suspicious activity reports on billions of dollars of transactions.\nIn addition, the bank paid an $11.6m fine to the treasury department’s office of foreign ⁠assets control ​for more than 400 apparent violations of numerous sanctions programs. The treasury said the bank mistakenly ​processed millions of dollars in payments that violated sanctions programs targeting countries including Russia and Iran.\nThe fine comes days after American Express\nwas also hit with a $350m penalty\nfor similar anti-money ​laundering shortcomings.\nExplore more on these topics\nBank of America\nBanking\nRegulators\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-15T00:02:46.794735", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Bank", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.487, "sm": 275, "em": 487, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "of", "s": 0.487, "e": 0.562, "sm": 487, "em": 562, "cs": 5, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "America", "s": 0.562, "e": 1.1, "sm": 562, "em": 1100, "cs": 8, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "was", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.275, "sm": 1100, "em": 1274, "cs": 16, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "fined", "s": 1.275, "e": 1.6, "sm": 1275, "em": 1599, "cs": 20, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "$", "s": 1.6, "e": 1.62, "sm": 1599, "em": 1619, "cs": 26, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "1.21", "s": 1.6, "e": 2